      "extract": "[]{#1 label=\"1\"} At low-energies the strong, electromagnetic and weak interactions of the lightest pseudoscalar mesons can be described by an effective chiral Lagrangian [@sw; @gl]. This Lagrangian depends on a number of coupling constants which are not fixed by symmetry requirements alone but are, in principle, determined by the dynamics of the underlying QCD theory. Recently, there have been attempts to derive the",
